# Playwright constitution

Apply on every test change. Examples live in `.cursor/rules/playwright-conventions.mdc`. Agent governance applies to every non-trivial task.

## Agent governance

Behavioral contract only. Do not enforce it with a hook.

Audit, then edit. Before editing on a non-trivial task, emit a Proposal block:

```text
Proposal
Scope:
Confidence: <1-10>
Rationale:
Unknowns:
```

| Confidence | Do |
|------------|----|
| Under 5 | Do not proceed. Ask for the missing input. |
| 5–7 | Proceed only with the unknowns written down and a human approval. |
| 8 or higher | Proceed. |

Never invent a path, enum, env var, credential, or message. Ask, or explore the repo and the live UI, instead.

## MUST

| Rule | Do |
|------|----|
| Role-based locators | `getByRole`, then label, placeholder, or text. `getByTestId` only with a comment. |
| Web-first assertions | `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` / `toBeEnabled()` / `toHaveText()` so the expect retries. |
| storageState auth | Session from the setup project. UI login only in the login spec. |
| Unique self-cleaning data | `` `${prefix} ${Date.now()}` ``, then `trackProgram(uuid)` so the fixture deletes it. |
| One strategy tag | Exactly one of `@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, `@destructive` on the `test()` call. |
| Revert shared state | A test that writes locale, roles, flags, or settings is `@destructive`, restores that value in `afterEach` or `afterAll`, and runs only via `test:destructive` (`--workers=1`). |

## SHOULD

| Rule | Do |
|------|----|
| Faker factories | Build records in a factory. |
| Enums for repeated strings | Shared labels, routes, and statuses live in an enum. |
| JSDoc on action methods | Each POM action states what the user does. |

## WON'T

| Never | Why |
|-------|-----|
| XPath | Breaks when the markup shifts and the control is unchanged. |
| `waitForTimeout` | Sleeps on the clock, so the test flakes or wastes time. |
| Hardcoded secrets | Credentials come from the environment and `storageState`. |
| The `any` type | Hides a bad payload until runtime. |
| Weakened assertions | Softening or deleting an expect to go green hides the failure. |
| Healing a real bug | Locator drift gets a POM patch. A product defect gets a Jira bug. |
| Tags on `describe` | A describe tag stamps every test in the block. Tag the test. |
| A second strategy tag | `@smoke` through `@destructive` are mutually exclusive. Own-record cleanup stays on the importance or lane tag. |
| `@destructive` for own data | Creating and deleting the test's own records is cleanup, not a shared setting. |

## Index

Skills: `a11y-checks`, `api-cleanup`, `ci-failure-triage`, `explore-and-generate`, `exploratory-charter`, `jira-bug-reporter`, `jira-ticket-to-gherkin`, `pom-conventions`, `programs-api-edges`, `self-heal`. Agents: `test-writer` (plan → spec), `triage` (red run → bug or test issue), `bug-reporter` (confirmed defect → Jira).
